    ],
    bottomLine: "The Merach most people should start with: a folding treadmill with real powered incline and room to walk briskly, for about $400.",
    description: "The T16 is the most rounded machine in Merach’s Amazon range. The listing describes it as a folding treadmill for walking, jogging and incline training, with 15 incline levels up to 15% changed by motor, so you can climb without stepping off. The belt is 43.5 by 16.5 inches with a five-layer anti-slip surface and six shock-absorbing pads, which is about an inch longer than the T12 and noticeably roomier than most walking pads. Merach gives a 3.0 HP brushless motor, speeds of 0.6 to 7.5 mph, a 300 lb capacity, controls on the console and handrails, P1 to P15 preset programs and app sync, and says the machine arrives almost fully assembled. Amazon lists the item weight at 92 lb. It was $399.98 on 9 November 2026. The limits are those of the whole range: 7.5 mph is an easy jog, not a run, and 43.5 inches is short for a long running stride. The bullet points we read mention no warranty term, so get it in writing from the seller before you order.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-t12-auto",
    name: "MERACH T12 Foldable Treadmill, 15% Auto Incline",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Compact folding treadmill with powered incline",
    badge: "Best Value Auto Incline",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F1L2BF59?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41u7e+DuBBL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $360 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":360,"high":360},
    specs: "15% auto incline · 42.5 x 16.5 in. belt · 0.5–7.5 mph · 2.5 HP · 300 lb capacity · folds to 49.2 x 25.6 x 27.6 in. · 1-year warranty",
    pros: [
      "Powered incline to 15% for about $40 less than the T16",
      "States its folded size, 49.2 by 25.6 by 27.6 inches",
      "Handrail heart-rate sensors and 12 preset programs",
      "Listing states a one-year warranty and lifetime support",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Shares its title with a manual-incline version; check the bullet points",
      "Belt an inch shorter than the T16’s",
      "Walking and easy jogging only at 7.5 mph",
    ],
    bottomLine: "A cheaper route to a powered 15% incline on a compact folding frame, if you buy the auto version and not its manual twin.",
    description: "The T12 is Merach’s compact folding treadmill, and this listing is the version with a powered incline. Its bullet points give a 0.5 to 7.5 mph speed range, a 15% auto incline and a 42.5 by 16.5-inch belt, with what Merach calls double-deck technology, four silicone shock cushions and six shock-absorbing pillars, built-in heart-rate sensors and a 300 lb maximum user weight. The motor is listed at 2.5 HP, and the listing claims under 40 dB of noise, a figure we could not check and would not rely on. The folded dimensions are given as 49.2 by 25.6 by 27.6 inches, with transport wheels, and there are 12 preset programs and app support. Merach states a one-year warranty and lifetime customer support. It was $359.98 on 9 November 2026. The catch is the name. The title reads “0-6/15% Manual/Auto Incline”, and the same title is used for a cheaper T12 with a three-position manual incline, so read the incline bullet before you buy.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-18-auto-incline",
    name: "MERACH Treadmill with 18% Auto Incline, 47 x 18 in. Belt",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Larger folding treadmill with steep powered incline",
    badge: "Longest Belt, Most Incline",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FVT465SQ?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41ndMxgNscL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $550 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":550,"high":550},
    specs: "18% auto incline · 47 x 18 in. belt · to 8.7 mph · 3.5 HP brushless (max) · 350 lb capacity · hydraulic folding",
    pros: [
      "The steepest incline in the range, 18%, powered",
      "A wider, longer 47 by 18-inch belt; a 55-inch version is about $100 more",
      "350 lb rating on a frame Merach says is 2.0 mm core steel",
      "Hydraulic folding and an app with coach plans",
    ],
    cons: [
      "At 8.7 mph, still not a running treadmill for most runners",
      "Heavy: the listing says it weighs 122 lb",
      "No warranty term in the bullet points we read",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The Merach for steep incline walking and easy jogging on a bigger deck, if you have the room and the budget.",
    description: "This is the largest Merach treadmill we found on Amazon, sold in two lengths under one title. The listing we read is the 47-inch version: an 18 by 47-inch belt, an 18% powered incline, a maximum 3.5 HP brushless motor, a top speed of 8.7 mph and a 350 lb capacity, with a frame Merach describes as 2.0 mm thick core steel and gives as weighing 122 lb. It folds with hydraulic assistance, has an LED display showing speed, time, distance, calories, incline and heart rate, and works with the Merach app. It was $549.99 on 9 November 2026. A 55 by 18-inch version, listed with 18 incline levels and three climbing modes, was $649.99, and Merach notes that its maximum incline may be slightly lower because of the longer deck. The longer deck is the one to choose if you want to jog. Neither version is a fast running machine, and the bullet points we read give no warranty term, so ask before you order.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-t12-manual",
    name: "MERACH T12 Foldable Treadmill, 6% Manual Incline",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Budget folding treadmill with manual incline",
    badge: "Cheapest Treadmill",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D878L9RZ?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41TIu45TLoL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
