          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you run on a Merach treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only lightly. The folding treadmills top out at 7.5 mph, or 8.7 mph on the larger 18-level model, and their belts are 42.5 to 55 inches long. That suits easy jogging for many people, but not running intervals or a long running stride. The walking pads stop at about 4 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Which Merach walking pad has the highest weight capacity?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The NovaWalk W50 and UltraWalk W60 are both listed at 400 lb. The W60’s listing adds that 400 lb is a peak figure and 330 lb is its sustained capacity, so plan on the lower figure. The W50 Lite is listed at 350 lb.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do Merach treadmills need the app?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. The folding treadmills run from their consoles and the walking pads from a remote. The Merach app adds scenic routes, coach plans and tracking, and the pad listings mention syncing with Apple Health and Google Fit.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

